> * v133: change to "stressed_hy_rafsi"
> <http://tiki.lojban.org/tiki/tiki-pagehistory.php?page=3DBPFK+Section%3A+=
PEG+Morphology+Algorithm&history_offset=3D0&diff_style=3Dsidediff&show_all_=
versions=3Dy&compare=3DCompare&newver=3D132&oldver=3D131&paginate=3Don&hist=
ory_pagesize=3D50&bothver_idx=3D49>
>

Hmm... the change to consonantal_syllable is wrong.


> Are people familiar with the theory behind this change? Is it acceptable?
> Or is there a reason that it was not propagated?
>

It was incorrect, because it makes the parser think that the "dn" in
"badnrgrute" is a consonantal syllable, but it isn't, it has to be
"bad,nr,gru,te"


> If it's not something that we want to keep, the BPFK morphology algorithm
> page should be updated to reflect that.
>

Done. I have changed it to:

consonantal-syllable <- consonant &syllabic coda


> On a related note, this might be a good time to start discussing the
> migration of the official BPFK work pages to the mediawiki.
>

I made the change in both wikis, just in case.

mu'o mi'e xorxes

